      "id": "ANC-001",
      "source_type": "ANC",
      "source_ref": null,
      "statement": "The template ships general database commands on the CLI, MCP, and HTTP, including delete row <table> <id>. The consumer can disable that surface. An application command calls the same backend operation through its own CLI command, MCP tool, and HTTP route.",
      "quote": "the 'general database commands' would be expected to be disabled by the customer. they are simply a bootstrap tool and could easily be 'replaced' w/ a command that has better ux and does a similar call on the back-end. i.e. delete row <table> <id> would be a general command which could be used 'under the hood' w/ a different cli/mcp/http call.",
      "kind": "directive",
      "stated_by": "randlee",
      "stated_at": "2026-10-25",
      "context": "planning session",
      "summary": "Bootstrap database commands the consumer can disable",
      "scope": "a bead that edits template CLI, MCP, or HTTP commands",
      "deterministic_check": "The generated template registers a general delete-row command on the CLI, on MCP, and over HTTP, and a generation flag omits those three registrations while the backend operation remains callable.",
